{"study_accession":"PRJNA542792","secondary_study_accession":"SRP198343","title":"Large, Diverse Population Cohorts of hiPSCs and Derived Hepatocyte-like Cells Reveal Functional Genetic Variation at Blood Lipid-Associated Loci","description":"Musunuru, Brown, Rader, and colleagues of the NHLBI NextGen consortium use multi-ethnic population cohorts of iPSCs and differentiated hepatocyte-like cells, in combination with mouse models, to discover and validate functional DNA variants and genes at blood lipid- associated loci previously identified by genome-wide association studies. Overall design: Peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs) isolated 91 individuals (43% African Americans and 55% European Americans; 60% women and 40% men) were used to generate iPSCs. PBMCs were differentiated into HLCs which were morphologically similar to primary hepatocytes. RNA-seq data was generated from iPSCs (n=89), HLCs (n=86), primary hepatocytes (n=4) and whole liver in GTEx cohort (n=96). The majority of data for this study is deposited in at dbGaP for controlled access: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/gap/?term=phs001341","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":4,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN11638247","study_accession":"PRJNA542792","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"study","title":"HU8164","description":"HU8164","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM3764823","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":18,"first_public":"2019-05-17","attributes":[["source_name","Primary hepatocytes"],["biomaterial_provider","Thermo Fisher Scientific"],["cell_type","Human plateable hepatocytes, Metabolism qualified"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR9051496","experiment_accession":"SRX5827769","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 2500","read_count":3395454,"base_count":848863500,"first_public":"2019-05-17","experiment_title":"Illumina HiSeq 2500 sequencing: GSM3764823: HU8164 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"},{"run_accession":"SRR9051497","experiment_a